{"result": "{\n    \"title\": \"Global Health Community: WHO, EU, and Health Law\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community encompasses key entities involved in global health, including the World Health Organization (WHO), the European Union (EU), and various health law frameworks. These entities are interconnected through their roles in establishing health standards, guidelines, and regulations that impact public health, nutrition, and patient rights across different regions.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the significant influence these entities have on global health policies and practices, which can affect millions of lives.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The WHO's pivotal role in global health\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The World Health Organization (WHO) is a central entity in this community, responsible for coordinating international public health efforts and establishing health standards. The WHO's guidelines cover a wide range of health issues, including nutrition, disease classification, and public health initiatives. For instance, the WHO has updated classifications for diseases such as craniofaringiomas and neuroendocrine tumors, which are crucial for accurate diagnosis and treatment. Additionally, the WHO provides comprehensive guidelines on nutrition, emphasizing the importance of proper dietary practices for vulnerable populations, including children and pregnant women. This extensive influence underscores the WHO's critical role in shaping global health policies and practices [Data: Entities (1262); Relationships (4789, 714, 1657, 5923, 5946, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The European Union's regulatory framework\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The European Union (EU) plays a significant role in shaping health and nutrition policies across its member states. It establishes comprehensive regulations that cover various aspects of health, including dietary reference intakes and food safety standards. The EU's collaboration with the WHO enhances its ability to implement effective health policies, ensuring that member states adhere to established guidelines. For example, the EU has incorporated the Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP) system into its food safety legislation, reinforcing its commitment to food quality and safety. This regulatory framework is essential for maintaining public health and ensuring that nutritional standards are met across Europe [Data: Entities (864); Relationships (5168, 5156, 5157, 5161, 5113, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Health law's influence on patient rights and nutrition\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Health law encompasses regulations and ethical standards that govern medical practices and patient rights, significantly impacting how health services are delivered. In Spain, for instance, health law is influenced by the Constitution and the regulations set by the European Union. This legal framework ensures that patients receive adequate care and that their rights are protected. Furthermore, health law addresses nutritional support, outlining ethical standards for patient care, particularly for vulnerable groups such as pregnant women and children. The interplay between health law and organizations like the WHO and the EU highlights the importance of legal frameworks in promoting public health and nutrition [Data: Entities (15799); Relationships (829, 20223, 20224, 20225, 20226, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Collaboration between WHO and other health organizations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The WHO collaborates with various organizations, including the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), to enhance global health initiatives. This collaboration allows for the sharing of data and best practices, which is crucial for addressing public health challenges. For example, the WHO and CDC work together to establish health standards for child growth, ensuring that guidelines are based on comprehensive data. Such partnerships are vital for developing effective health policies and interventions that can be implemented worldwide [Data: Entities (13792); Relationships (5960, 5961, 5964, 5965, 5966, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of nutritional guidelines on public health\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Nutritional guidelines established by the WHO and the EU play a crucial role in improving public health outcomes. These guidelines address various health issues, including obesity, malnutrition, and dietary practices. For instance, the WHO provides recommendations on sugar intake and dietary fiber, which are essential for maintaining health and preventing chronic diseases. The emphasis on nutrition in public health policies reflects the understanding that dietary habits significantly influence overall health. By promoting healthy eating practices, these organizations aim to reduce the prevalence of diet-related diseases and improve the quality of life for populations worldwide [Data: Entities (8000); Relationships (5946, 5924, 5929, 5930, 5931, +more)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1262,OMS,\"The OMS (Organización Mundial de la Salud), known in English as the World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for coordinating international public health efforts. The OMS plays a crucial role in establishing health standards, providing guidelines, and conducting research on various health-related topics. It is involved in the classification of diseases, including specific conditions such as craniofaringiomas and neuroendocrine tumors, and has updated its classifications, notably in 2017 for pituitary tumors.\n\nThe OMS provides comprehensive guidelines on a wide range of health issues, including the management of acute diarrhea, nutritional needs, and dietary recommendations. It emphasizes the importance of proper nutrition for children, pregnant women, and lactating mothers, advocating for a varied diet that meets all necessary nutrient requirements. The organization also offers formulas for estimating energy expenditure and dietary needs, which are essential for understanding the nutritional status of different populations.\n\nIn addition to its focus on nutrition, the OMS addresses broader health topics such as active aging, telemedicine, and the use of information and communication technologies in healthcare. It provides guidelines for rehydration solutions and has developed international reference patterns for child growth, contributing to global health initiatives aimed at improving the quality of life.\n\nThe OMS is recognized for its leadership in global health matters, shaping the health research agenda, and providing critical data on health issues such as diabetes prevalence and obesity management. Through its extensive guidelines and recommendations, the OMS aims to optimize health opportunities and enhance the overall well-being of populations worldwide.\",69\r\n15799,DERECHO SANITARIO,Health law encompasses regulations and ethical standards that govern medical practices and patient rights.,6\r\n942,FIGURA 8,\"FIGURA 8 is a multifaceted entity that encompasses both culinary and scientific aspects. It features an illustration that showcases vegetables cooked to an al dente texture, which serves as a demonstration of the proper cooking technique for dysphagia diets, ensuring that individuals with swallowing difficulties can enjoy nutritious meals safely. Additionally, FIGURA 8 includes the World Health Organization's equations for estimating energy expenditure, providing a scientific framework for understanding energy needs. This combination of culinary guidance and health-related equations highlights FIGURA 8's role in promoting both dietary health and nutritional awareness.\",2\r\n864,UNIÓN EUROPEA,\"The Unión Europea (European Union, EU) is a political and economic union comprising 27 member states located primarily in Europe. It aims to promote integration and cooperation among its members while establishing a comprehensive framework of regulations and directives that cover various aspects of health, nutrition, and food safety. The EU is responsible for setting guidelines related to health and nutrition, including dietary reference intakes and nutritional guidelines for its member states. \n\nIn addition to health and nutrition, the Unión Europea regulates food safety through the establishment of norms concerning food quality, safety, and the use of food additives. It oversees legislation that impacts health law and patient rights across its member states, ensuring that standards are maintained, including those for infant formulas. The EU has also emphasized the importance of defining frailty, particularly in relation to healthcare resources and elderly care.\n\nFurthermore, the Unión Europea has incorporated the Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP) system into its food safety legislation, reinforcing its commitment to ensuring the safety and quality of food products. Overall, the Unión Europea plays a crucial role in shaping health and nutrition policies, as well as food safety regulations, across its member states.\",17\r\n1306,BRASIL,Brasil es un país que proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y la nutrición en el contexto de la Organización Mundial de la Salud (OMS).,2\r\n7870,MUJERES EMBARAZADAS,\"Mujeres embarazadas are pregnant women who undergo monitoring for anemia, a condition that can affect their health and the health of their unborn child. During pregnancy, these women may require iron supplementation to address any deficiencies and ensure a healthy pregnancy.\",5\r\n13792,CDC,\"The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) is a national public health institute in the United States that plays a crucial role in providing health guidelines and standards. It is responsible for disseminating information related to health and safety, including specific growth patterns for children. The CDC's mission encompasses a wide range of public health initiatives aimed at improving the overall health of the population.\",4\r\n4822,FUNDACIÓN SEEN,\"La Fundación SEEN es una organización que se dedica a la investigación y promoción de la salud endocrina en España, incluyendo el estudio de trastornos por déficit de yodo.\",3\r\n5459,CIE-11,\"The CIE-11, or Clasificación Internacional de Enfermedades (International Classification of Diseases), is the 11th revision of a comprehensive classification system designed to categorize diseases and health conditions. It was presented at the World Health Assembly in May 2019 for adoption by Member States. This classification system includes parameters specifically for the evaluation of nutritional status, highlighting its role in assessing various health aspects beyond just diseases.\",2\r\n15268,NCHS,\"The National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) is an organization that provides data on the growth and nutrition of school-aged children and adolescents in the United States. However, it is important to note that the NCHS was replaced by the CDC's 2000 growth standards in the United States, indicating a shift in the authority and standards used for assessing growth and nutrition in this demographic.\",2\r\n15269,BRAZIL,Brazil is one of the countries included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children.,1\r\n8735,DI@BET.ES,Di@bet.es is an organization that conducts research on obesity and its related health issues.,1\r\n15267,EURO-GROWTH 2000,Euro-Growth 2000 is a multicentric study that established growth patterns for European children aged 0-5 years.,1\r\n15271,GHANA,\"Ghana is a country that plays a significant role in providing data on child growth and nutrition within the context of the World Health Organization (WHO). It is included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children, which contributes to the global understanding of child growth. Through its participation, Ghana aids in the development of comprehensive insights into the nutritional status and growth patterns of children, thereby supporting global health initiatives.\",1\r\n4837,GINEBRA,\"Ginebra es una ciudad en Suiza, sede de la Organización Mundial de la Salud, donde se realizan importantes reuniones sobre salud global.\",1\r\n15276,GURNEY AND JELLIFFE,Gurney and Jelliffe are referenced for their nomogram used to calculate muscle area in nutritional assessments.,1\r\n15270,INDIA,\"India is a country that plays a significant role in providing data on child growth and nutrition within the context of the World Health Organization (WHO). It is also included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children, contributing to global standards and understanding of child health and development.\",1\r\n4840,M,M es un autor que ha investigado sobre la nutrición y el yodo durante el embarazo y la lactancia.,1\r\n4839,MA KOMINIAREK,MA Kominiarek es un autor que ha escrito sobre recomendaciones nutricionales en el embarazo y la lactancia